  "reason": "The exact pinned candidate forms a continuous layered limestone face along the declared N upper-right diagonal, remains a narrow height-1 boundary at runtime scale, and matches the cave reference stratified rock vocabulary. Unlike the rejected E variant, it has no meaningful detached fragment: one 3,259-pixel component contains the visible subject; the only separate nonzero-alpha island is two faint antialias pixels and is not visibly discernible. Normalization is current and detects only N. Coverage is 49 per mille with 128x82 bounds and transparent corners; all three seam thirds have sustained contact within 6 pixels, and endpoints are within 7 pixels and 8.1 pixels.",
